  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math>-block elements form coloured ions due to presence of unpaired electrons in them. since there are no unpaired electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sc</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions, they are colourless.</p><p>No of unpaired <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ti</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sc</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mo>]</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>No d-d transitions in ions with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></math> configuration. Therefore they are colourless.</p></blockquote>",
